{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1458719-true-fae-characters","id":1458719,"title":"True Fae characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-04T13:35:12-07:00","id":1458719,"title":"True Fae characters","content":"In <b><i>Changeling: The Lost </i></b>I would like to see the True Fae/Gentry be given a larger role in the story and allow players to confront/fight their Keeper. While the 2E core book does give the storyteller a general idea of how to do this, I would like a 2E Autumn Nightmares book that gives greater detail on the powers and abilities of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> One way I did this was through drawing on 1e True Fae titles and inspiration from Pennywise/It from the Stephen King novel. The idea is that Titles are manifestations of human fairytales, folklore, mythology, and superstitions. However, 21C Hermit pointed out that this is closer to <b><i>Beasts: The Primordial </i></b>and True Fae are not necessarily fairytales monsters and entities. My explanation is that the True Fae are not limited to one title or form. For example, I have a True Fae/Gentry who is a manifestation of the fairytale concept <i>Prince Charming, </i>the fairytale <i>Beauty and the Beast,</i> AND is the Oberon from <i>Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream. </i><br /> <br /> Plus, there are many variations of some of our most popular folktales and fairytales change overtime. This could be another reason are not the EXACT monsters and demons of myths.<br /> <br /> When you introduce/use Gentry/True Fae in your chronicles, how do you guys build/develop them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T19:25:45-07:00","id":1458762,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer True Fae to be statless antagonists, as in &quot;I didn't give this thing any stats other than a Wyrd score because you WILL lose if you fight it head-on.&quot; The Wyrd score is mostly for determining what Regalia it has.<br /> <br /> For something that the changelings can challenge in direct confrontation, I prefer using Huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T21:21:44-07:00","id":1458774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1458719-true-fae-characters?p=1458762#post1458762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prefer True Fae to be statless antagonists, as in &quot;I didn't give this thing any stats other than a Wyrd score because you WILL lose if you fight it head-on.&quot; The Wyrd score is mostly for determining what Regalia it has.<br /> <br /> For something that the changelings can challenge in direct confrontation, I prefer using Huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless the changeling is of high wyrd, I don't think they should be able to defeat the True Fae Through brute force. I am in favor of giving them frailties connected to the themes associated with their titles. Think of how the Loser gang from <b><i>It </i></b>beat Pennywise.<br /> <br /> For example, the True Fae is described above is supposed to represent the ideals of True Love. However, he is too selfish to truly represent that ideal. So, all the changelings who escape from him have someone they love AND the characters who can beat him are motivated by love. Not necessarily romantic love, but the love of a parent for a child, a strong bond between friends or siblings ect.<br /> <br /> I tried to portray that in the titles I created for the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T22:59:36-07:00","id":1458784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1458719-true-fae-characters?p=1458762#post1458762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prefer True Fae to be statless antagonists, as in &quot;I didn't give this thing any stats other than a Wyrd score because you WILL lose if you fight it head-on.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically tried to design True Fae titles, so if the character tried to fight the Gentry head on, the TRUE FAE WOULD STOMP THEM LIKE SUMO BELLY DANCERS. Monster allows you to do +3 aggravated damage with unarmed attacks and Fairest of them all is essentially a jacked up version of Majesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T23:46:17-07:00","id":1459512,"title":"","content":"I used mostly the rules and ideas in Equinox Road, with some tweaking here and there, but I didn't had a chronicle in 2E yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}